- ACTIVE COMBAT — MECHANICAL EVALUATION SCOPE: Identify only which dice rolls (if any) this domain requires for the player's declared action (attack rolls, saves, skill checks, concentration, etc.). Do not fully adjudicate hits, damage, flanking, AoO geometry, full-attack sequencing, or multi-target spell resolution here — the Combat GM step owns that synthesis when combat is active.
- Leave npc_actions EMPTY during routine combat rounds. World turn resolves NPC initiative actions after the player. Only include an npc_action here when the player's action triggers an immediate reaction that must be queued before rolls resolve (extremely rare).
- Reference combat context for turn order and participant names only as needed to phrase roll requests.
